// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27os/account_view.t27 -- what the ACCOUNT panel of the T27 OS window shows and what a click in it means. Pure
// decisions only: no @extern, no socket, no clock. One place where a person sees themselves (picture, nickname), their
// own key (the T27-... string a friend pastes), the state of this device (online or not, the port, the build) and the
// friends (online or not, the unread count, open the friend's card with MESSAGE / CALL / VIDEO (chat_view.t27), copy
// the key, remove after a confirmation, add by key). Owner, 2026-10-22: the person
// copies their key, sends it to a friend by any means, the friend pastes it and calls; no address is ever typed.
// Refs gHashTag/t27#11560.
//
// Owner, 2026-10-22 (second pass): the cabinet opens on three things, in this order down the 300 pt panel.
//   ME     the picture, the nickname, the account token (the first three groups of the fingerprint, large), the key
//          a friend pastes with COPY beside it, what that key is for, and where the account lives (this device only:
//          T27 OS has no server account).
//   KEYS   one line a provider (OpenRouter, Z.ai, NVIDIA): how many keys, how many live, the reason of the dead ones,
//          when the last check was. Read from the tables the window already holds (the health words of keys.t27 and
//          the NVIDIA counts of nvidia_direct.t27); never a key value, never a request from this panel. A limit or a
//          balance is not in any of these tables, so the line shows none.
//   INVITATIONS (owner, 2026-10-22; only while there is one) people who added this device's key and wrote: the
//          newest AC_INV_ROWS_MAX, each with its nickname (the peer's own word), its short key, when it came and
//          "again" after a decline; ACCEPT makes it a friend (its proven key stored), DECLINE hides it (invites.t27).
//          The number waiting stands in the head as well. The friends part moves down by ac_inv_dy.
//   CALL   the friends, online or not, with CALL and MESSAGE on every row; CALL in the head of the panel as well
//          while there is a friend, so a call is one click from the open cabinet.
// A long value is cut with an ellipsis at a code point (ac_fit), never past the panel's right edge.
//
// The panel is the IDLE view of the CALL panel's slot in a second mode (AC_ON = 1 in the CALL region of the text
// store): the call views, the friends snapshot (friends_view), the engine (friends_engine) and the typing of the add
// field are the ones of the CALL panel; PROFILE (profile.t27) keeps the picture. A call that rings or is up shows
// its own view over the ACCOUNT mode and gives the panel back when it is dismissed.
//
// The key of a friend is made from the 10-byte fingerprint of the table row (invite_make): the same string the friend
// copies from their own panel, check symbol included. "Online" means what friends_view says it means.
// Flat namespace (the window build splices imported modules): every name here starts with ac_ / AC_.
module T27osAccountView;

